There are different ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement:

If your program has a main function, you can use the return statement to terminate the program. The value returned by the main function is the exit status of the program.

```c
int main() {
    // Your code here
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function:

The exit() function is a standard library function that terminates the execution of the program immediately. It takes an integer argument which is the exit status of the program.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your code here
    exit(0);
    return 0;
}
```

3. Using the return 0; statement outside the main function:

If your program has multiple functions, you can use the return 0; statement outside the main function to terminate the program. This is not a recommended way of terminating a program as it is not standard practice and may not work on all systems.

```c
int main() {
    // Your code

